[32m+[m[32m## Shipping — Velocity Integration: PENDING / BLOCKED BY API DOCUMENTATION (added 2026-09-12)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Status: on hold. No Velocity-specific code exists in this repo — none should be added until real API documentation is supplied.** The current flat-rate `ShippingZone`/`ShippingRate` checkout flow (see below) is untouched and must stay untouched until this is unblocked.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Why it's blocked**: a repo-wide search found zero references to a "Velocity" shipping/logistics API anywhere in this codebase (the only two hits for the word are unrelated — inside the Swiper carousel and parallax-scroll third-party JS libraries). There are multiple logistics companies with similar names; guessing endpoints, auth headers, or payload shapes would mean shipping fabricated integration code, which was explicitly ruled out.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**What's needed before implementation can start** — official Velocity documentation (link, PDF, or Postman collection) covering:[m
[32m+[m[32m- API base URL (and whether test/sandbox vs. production use different hosts)[m
[32m+[m[32m- Authentication method (API key header, OAuth, HMAC-signed requests, etc.)[m
[32m+[m[32m- Serviceability API (check if a PIN/postal code is deliverable)[m
